  <title>7.11.7: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01921</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.11.7: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2bf4a714-db19-4bf5-97e0-6aed27696a2b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>To help students consolidate the ideas in this lesson, consider asking them to reflect on some or all of the following questions in writing or by discussing with a partner:</para>
<para>A quadratic function \(k\) is defined by \(k(x)=(x-100)(x+20)\). How would you explain to a friend who is absent today how to use the equation to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Find the zeros of the function? </item>
  <item> Find the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph? </item>
  <item> Find the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex without graphing? </item>
  <item> Find the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex without graphing? </item>
  <item> Find the \(y\)-intercept of the graph? </item>
</list></section>
</content>
